      "writtenOn": "2021-02-04T16:23:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e We believe find_lowest_rq() hook is the best place to implement any vendor changes as we go through that path from RT load balancer (push \u0026 pull algo) and we also will have lowest_mask available at that time which avoids duplication of code. We don\u0027t really need multiple hooks in case of RT.\n\nUnderstood, but nothing prevents you from calling your own version find_lowest_rq() unconditonally from your own version of select_task_rq_rt().\n\n\u003e Also, IMHO, we should always invoke find_lowest_rq() when respective hook is enabled irrespective of select_task_rq_rt hook is registered or not to find suitable CPU than just sticking to previous CPU.\n\nWe have no good ways to ensure the entire ecosystem agrees, so I would prefer to not have functional changes in that code path if we can given that there is an alternative (the other hook).",
      "parentUuid": "175b11ba_6a1ebb74",
